From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 15:20:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] module: keep dynamic Syms out of module state after link

An embedder that truncates the interner between parse batches must know
when a registered module still holds its AST. Those ASTs hold
post-checkpoint Syms and make truncation unsafe. 0.22 drops the AST
itself once a module links, so the source is pending exactly in the
Unlinked and Linking states.

ResolveExport and GetExportedNames run at namespace-access time, at any
point in a module's life, and resolved their entry names through the
context interner on every call. That made the retained entry lists the
one place a dynamic Sym outlived its parse batch, which an embedder
truncating the interner trips over as a namespace-get panic ("binding is
a ResolvedBinding Record: NotFound").

Convert the local/indirect export entries to owned JsString names at
SourceTextModule construction, where the interner is in hand; star
entries already were. Import entries stay Sym-based: they are only read
during link, while the module still holds its AST (which is what gates
the embedder's truncation). The interner parameter disappears from the
whole resolve_export/get_exported_names call graph, so nothing can
quietly reintroduce a runtime Sym read.

A re-export entry also carries import attributes, so it holds its
resolved ModuleRequest instead of rebuilding it from Syms on every
resolve.
